      "text": "For all real c > 0 and e > 0 and any real h, with growth(p) = c p (h - p) - e p and p* = h - e/c, the following hold. (1) growth(p) = c p (p* - p) for every p. (2) If h <= e/c, then growth(p) < 0 for every p > 0. (3) If e/c < h, then 0 < p* < h, growth(p*) = 0, growth > 0 on (0, p*) and growth < 0 for every p > p*. (4) e/c < h iff 1 - h < 1 - e/c. (5) e/c is strictly decreasing in c and strictly increasing in e.",
